.TH NFS-CACHEFS 8 "2026-10-31" "nfs-cachefs 1.1" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
nfs-cachefs \- userspace daemon for Linux fscache + cachefiles (traditional mode)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nfs-cachefs
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-log-level\fR \fILEVEL\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nfs-cachefs
is a modern Rust replacement for the upstream
.BR cachefilesd (8)
daemon. It opens
.I /dev/cachefiles ,
configures the kernel
.B cachefiles
backend, and drives cache culling by deleting LRU objects when the cache
filesystem approaches its
.B bcull
or
.B fcull
thresholds.

The daemon does not handle cache hits or misses on the data path \(em that
is done entirely by the kernel
.BR cachefiles.ko
module. NFS clients mounted with
.B \-o\ fsc
will transparently populate and read from the local cache filesystem
configured here.

This implementation supports the traditional userspace protocol only.
On-demand mode (kernel \(>=\ 5.19,
.BR CONFIG_CACHEFILES_ONDEMAND ) is not supported by this binary; on
distributions that ship with
.B CONFIG_CACHEFILES_ONDEMAND=n
(e.g. Ubuntu 24.04) only the traditional mode is available anyway.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR
TOML configuration file. Default:
.IR /etc/nfs-cachefs/daemon.toml .
.TP
\fB\-\-log-level\fR \fILEVEL\fR
Log level (\fIerror\fR, \fIwarn\fR, \fIinfo\fR, \fIdebug\fR,
\fItrace\fR). Takes precedence over
.BR RUST_LOG ,
which takes precedence over the configuration file.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The shipped
.I daemon.toml
documents every key; in short:
.TP
.BR cache_dir ", " tag ", " secctx
Cache directory (its own mount point), cache tag, optional security
context.
.TP
.B max_size
Size budget for the cache, enforced as an XFS or ext4 project quota on
.BR cache_dir ,
which then reports the budget as its size to the kernel. Needs a
filesystem mounted with project quotas. Applied before the cache is bound;
changes take effect at the next start.
.TP
.B quota_project_id
Project ID for
.BR max_size .
Nothing else on the filesystem may use it.
.TP
.B extsize
XFS extent size hint inherited by new cache files.
.TP
.BR [limits] " brun, bcull, bstop, frun, fcull, fstop"
Free-space and free-inode percentages: culling starts below
.IR cull ,
stops at
.IR run ;
the kernel stops caching below
.IR stop .
.TP
.BR [cull] " batch_size"
Candidates kept per walk of the cache before object sizes are known.
.TP
.BR [metrics] " textfile, interval_secs, usage_scan_interval_secs"
Prometheus text file for node_exporter's textfile collector, and how
often to rewrite it.
.TP
.BR [log] " level, format"
Log level and format (\fIcompact\fR or \fIjson\fR).
.SH SIGNALS
.BR SIGTERM ,
.BR SIGINT " and"
.B SIGHUP
stop the daemon: it closes
.IR /dev/cachefiles ,
and the kernel withdraws the cache.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 after a requested stop, 2 for an unusable configuration or command
line, 1 otherwise \(em including when the kernel has stopped the cache
after an I/O error, so that the service manager starts the daemon, and
binds the cache, again.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/nfs-cachefs/daemon.toml
Configuration file.
When changing
.B cache_dir
under the packaged systemd unit, update the unit's
.B ReadWritePaths=
setting to match (the installer's drop-in
.IR /etc/systemd/system/nfs-cachefs.service.d/local.conf ).
.TP
.I /run/nfs-cachefs/
Writable for the daemon under the packaged unit; the suggested place for
.BR metrics.textfile .
.TP
.I /dev/cachefiles
Kernel control device.
.TP
.I /proc/fs/fscache/stats
Real-time fscache counters; useful for monitoring cache hit rates.
.TP
.I /proc/fs/fscache/caches
Lists caches; the daemon's
.B tag
appears here with state
.B A
while active and
.B E
after the kernel stopped it for an I/O error.
.TP
.I /proc/fs/nfsfs/volumes
Lists NFS mounts; the
.B FSC
column shows which mounts have caching enabled.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Tracing-subscriber filter directive.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cachefilesd (8),
.BR mount.nfs (8),
.BR xfs_quota (8)
.PP
.B Documentation/filesystems/caching/cachefiles.rst
in the Linux kernel source.
